  "summary": "Six preprints from mid-November 2026 tie Hall plateaus, anomalous Hall metals and nonlinear transport to quantum geometry, disorder and interactions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how band geometry, interactions and disorder determine Hall-type and related transport responses in topological and narrow-band materials. Studies address layer-dependent disorder controlling integer and fractional Chern plateau widths in twisted bilayer MoTe2, quantum geometry enabling altermagnetic and nematic order in narrow bands, and interaction-driven pseudospin order with anomalous Hall metals in Bernal-stacked tetralayer graphene. Others extend transport theory: multi-Weyl magnetotransport beyond the constant relaxation-time approximation, quantum-geometric nonlinear conductivity in SrTiO3 electron gases comparing (001) and (111) interfaces, and a 3D quantum anomalous Hall system where Chern numbers alone fail to characterize chiral responses. The new element is treating geometry and realistic disorder or interactions as explicit determinants of response. All six are preprints and theoretical or numerical in the summaries given.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
